    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Gunnar,<br><br>From the sem() help file:<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;<br><code>sample.cov.rescale</code>\r\n\r\n<p>If <code>TRUE</code>, the sample covariance matrix provided\r\nby the user is internally rescaled by multiplying it with a factor (N-1)/N.\r\nIf <code>&quot;default&quot;</code>, the value is set depending on the estimator and the\r\nlikelihood option: it is set to <code>TRUE</code> if maximum likelihood \r\nestimation is used and <code>likelihood=&quot;normal&quot;</code>, and <code>FALSE</code> \r\notherwise.</p>&gt;&gt;&gt;<br><br>If you override the default, you get the same matrix:<br><br>m1tfit &lt;- sem(model, sample.cov=m1t.cov, sample.nobs=200, fixed.x=FALSE, <br>  sample.cov.rescale=FALSE)<br><br>summary(m1tfit, standardized = TRUE)<br>lavInspect(m1tfit, &quot;cov.all&quot;)<br>lavInspect(m1tfit, &quot;sampstat&quot;)<br>m1t.cov<br><br>Keith Markus<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
